  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I found no past ticket that reports this exact problem. Your shortcut `Alt (Right)` + `è` mapped to `[` still types only `è`. The closest tickets are related but don't match. PowerToys#3641 explains that on layouts with AltGr, Windows treats `Alt (Right)` as `Ctrl (Left)` + `Alt (Right)`, and Keyboard Manager handles that combination badly. PowerToys#16570 covers a similar Mac-style AltGr remap on a Czech layout, but its symptom is different. As a workaround, try a shortcut that doesn't use AltGr, for example `Ctrl (Left)` + `Alt (Left)` + `è`, or a different modifier. Please also upload a PowerToys bug report ZIP, and state your keyboard layout (for example Italian or Swiss). That will help the team investigate this as a new report.\"}",
